# Sandbox vs IDE runtime

Two AWS contexts. **No shared filesystem.**

1. **Firecracker sandboxes** — agent execution, worktrees, publication exports. Use **sandbox API routes**.
2. **Orca IDE sessions** — browser IDE, terminals, Git, user-launched agent CLIs. Anything `codex resume` or a terminal must see uses **`/ide` file and execution routes**.

Do not write sandbox files expecting the IDE to see them, or the reverse.
Web app = Vercel control plane. Do not move control-plane work into AWS or IDE-session work onto Vercel serverless as a shortcut.
